ziWgt2ohCKqUTXSDx0vemopW-nK8-BxMswVlZQW67WSrHvGsza1ZHzXE3jmHjMvo1quwF-ejeu-YzC0-m0eWCG2ZoFtoIS7-3Zlj51eYU9t0ITbZ7zGV9xBr02EgVGLIqr24VHYc7mYEdiUe597dRiJj7Qn55aYYAbR6TU51ydYlZG0xbfLlfyuq3h-ZoIgdKXxnVzPu1GuvljF2lC9Xw9V-xUSG7cirfaA4owliy6_rAw_Yzpyxkc3qMG0STyJzNSfWUSszc1nX4IKelyjAy2OJSPJDY1McOU4ljm2AiP1BdmfJXqrxTfZBz-cwSQojYreYcJLGmwLcbBB1Iats3YE0zkDWv91-W8I7pYjx-fkh5RzCB0pW_OrDvY7dsZBzjBtehFgUrLdD7xvPfjV-IMoN07POCItjAHbZNqzfK0CGbOZM6XasOhzNF8_oUu4RXLPfmfoyWWN7Vi2b2iSumcWKA3XZBzNT5k-yfaGkADEaVYJ0jSeTHvEqf2tBB-jCwp68KnjBoLg9pKxpzOQfPdI-9oLr7jWgULEnAxNh4rlESj4wrpqwwolLzEYxRWs5-ViM6joy9HGa9eqW4YLW3iIBjFXrCmXPJg4t6GZ0yKpBlIPxiXMmUif7eKkY5AjFj_wiJO7ItdZ-IbaEGytIO1kYd"},{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_0bfe6e1fa8f24ccf016adb3bad5cd88191aa091fdf590d4450","call_id":"call_f3b645fd98414b638d7b40fc12a42f4f","name":"check_artifact","arguments":"{\"artifact_json\":\"{\\\"base_candidate\\\":3,\\\"patches\\\":[{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/inputs\\\",\\\"value\\\":[\\\"H001\\\",\\\"H002\\\",\\\"H003\\\",\\\"M001\\\",\\\"M002\\\",\\\"M003\\\",\\\"M004\\\",\\\"M005\\\",\\\"M006\\\",\\\"M007\\\"]},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/0/uses\\\",\\\"value\\\":[\\\"H003\\\",\\\"M001\\\",\\\"M004\\\",\\\"M005\\\",\\\"M006\\\"]},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/1/uses\\\",\\\"value\\\":[\\\"H001\\\",\\\"H002\\\",\\\"M001\\\",\\\"M002\\\",\\\"M003\\\",\\\"M007\\\"]},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/1/text\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"For fixed r and each j define g_j(x)=u_t(x,r)·u_{x_j}(x,r). The factors and their derivatives vanish outside C, so g_j and ∂_j g_j are smooth and compactly supported; M001 proves their integrability. Product differentiation gives ∂_j g_j=(∂_j u_t)·u_{x_j}+u_t·u_{x_jx_j}, with each dot product the finite sum over m components. For fixed other coordinates y, z↦g_j(x(y,z)) is smooth and zero for |z|>L. Apply M007 with u(z)=g_j(x(y,z)), v(z)=1, u′(z)=∂_j g_j(x(y,z)), v′(z)=0, endpoints −L,L. Both functions are continuous on the closed interval, differentiable in its interior, and their derivatives are interval-integrable because they are continuous there; M007 therefore gives ∫_{−L}^L ∂_j g_j dz=g_j(L)−g_j(−L)=0. The derivative vanishes outside this interval, so its whole-line integral on each coordinate fiber is zero. For n=1 the other-coordinate space is the singleton ℝ⁰. The coordinate-permuted derivative is continuous compactly supported, hence product-integrable by M001. Coordinate permutation preserves Lebesgue measure (it permutes orthonormal coordinate axes); the factor Lebesgue measures are σ-finite, hence S-finite, and ℝ is real normed, so M003 identifies its whole-space integral with the iterated integral, equal to zero. Thus ∫∂_j g_j=0 and ∫(∂_j u_t)·u_{x_j}=−∫u_t·u_{x_jx_j}; all fields are integrable by M001. Differentiate the exact Frobenius energy formula: e_t=2u_t·u_{tt}+2Σ_j u_{x_j}·∂_j u_t. Finite sums commute with integration. Summing the integration-by-parts identities and using Δ_xu=Σ_j u_{x_jx_j} gives E′(r)=2∫u_t·(u_{tt}−Δ_xu). Differentiating H001 gives 2u·u_t=0, hence u·u_t=0. At the same point H002 supplies a scalar a with u_{tt}−Δ_xu=a u. Inner product with u_t gives u_t·(u_{tt}−Δ_xu)=a(u_t·u)=0. The zero integrand is integrable, so E′(r)=0. No regularity of a is used; r>0 was arbitrary.\\\"},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"add\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/applications/-\\\",\\\"value\\\":{\\\"input\\\":\\\"M005\\\",\\\"at\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"bindings\\\":\\\"X=ℝⁿ, Y=ℝ, s=C, t=J, product identified with C×J.\\\",\\\"hypothesis_checks\\\":[\\\"ℝⁿ and ℝ carry their Euclidean topologies.\\\",\\\"C is compact by its witness basis H003.\\\",\\\"J=[r/2,3r/2] is compact as a closed bounded interval.\\\"]}},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"add\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/applications/-\\\",\\\"value\\\":{\\\"input\\\":\\\"M006\\\",\\\"at\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"bindings\\\":\\\"α=ℝⁿ, μ=Lebesgue, 𝕜=ℝ, E=ℝ, x₀=r, s=(r/2,3r/2), F(τ)(x)=e(x,τ), F′(τ)(x)=e_t(x,τ), bound(x)=K·1_C(x).\\\",\\\"hypothesis_checks\\\":[\\\"r belongs to the open interval (r/2,3r/2), so it is a neighborhood of x₀.\\\",\\\"For every τ in that interval F(τ) is continuous, hence measurable and a.e. strongly measurable.\\\",\\\"F(r)=e(·,r) is integrable by M001 using continuity and compact support.\\\",\\\"F′(r)=e_t(·,r) is continuous and thus a.e. strongly measurable.\\\",\\\"On compact C×J the continuous e_t is bounded by finite K; outside C it vanishes. Therefore |F′(τ)(x)|≤K·1_C(x) for all x,τ in the interval.\\\",\\\"K·1_C is integrable: C is compact measurable of finite Lebesgue measure and the function is bounded with support in C.\\\",\\\"Smoothness gives τ↦e(x,τ) derivative e_t(x,τ) for every x and τ in the interval.\\\"]}},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"add\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/applications/-\\\",\\\"value\\\":{\\\"input\\\":\\\"M007\\\",\\\"at\\\":\\\"S002\\\",\\\"bindings\\\":\\\"A=ℝ, a=−L, b=L, u(z)=g_j(x(y,z)), v(z)=1, u′(z)=∂_j g_j(x(y,z)), v′(z)=0, for each j and fixed remaining coordinates y.\\\",\\\"hypothesis_checks\\\":[\\\"u and v are continuous on uIcc(−L,L) by smoothness.\\\",\\\"u and v are differentiable on the open interval with the stated derivatives.\\\",\\\"u′ and v′ are interval-integrable since continuous on the compact interval.\\\",\\\"The scalar field ℝ has the complete normed algebra structure required.\\\",\\\"The endpoint values u(±L) are zero since C lies in the box and g_j vanishes outside C; v(±L)=1.\\\",\\\"M007 yields the interval integral of u′v+uv′ as the endpoint difference, here zero.\\\"]}}]}\"}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"在固定 mathlib 的 Lean 源码中搜索正则表达式，返回至多 100 行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"读取固定 mathlib 中一个 Mathlib/...lean 文件的指定行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"line_count":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start_line","line_count"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read an explicitly frozen task document by ID; no other local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_yui","description":"Read declared Yui rules/templates; no tests, historical runs or personal files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_artifact","description":"Check a JSON artifact against the explicit stage contract; this is not automatic mathematical certification.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_artifact","description":"Submit a JSON artifact after its stage checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"report_obstacle","description":"Report exact status, location, explanation, basis, partial_progress. SUBSTANTIVE_GAP or SUSPECTED_GAP stops for an actual unsupported mathematical implication; give its premises, conclusion and mathematical grounds. SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE or INPUT_CONFLICT stops for a real source-access/original-input obstacle. Ordinary unfinished drafting, source registration or format work must use TASK_INCOMPLETE: this records progress without ending the stage; continue the actual work. Difficulty or artifact incompletion alone is not a mathematical gap.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"obstacle_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["obstacle_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"probe_library","description":"Query a proved Mathlib theorem and its exact signature/axioms in the offline sandbox. Returns located evidence for an M source; the mathematical statement and applicability still require review.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"declaration":{"type":"string"},"module":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","declaration","module"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_draft","description":"Read a JSON pointer in your own same-stage candidate after an actual structural check. No other file/stage is accessible; choose a narrow pointer for large objects.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"candidate":{"type":"integer"},"pointer":{"type":"string"}},"required":["candidate","pointer"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false}],"tool_choice":"auto","parallel_tool_calls":false,"prompt_cache_key":"9ceaaf4f-fc71-46fc-8ec3-d580912f0fa4","prompt_cache_retention":"24h","text":{"format":{"type":"text"},"verbosity":"low"},"top_p":0.98,"top_logprobs":0,"temperature":1.0,"reasoning":{"effort":"high","context":"all_turns","summary":null,"mode":"standard"},"user":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":58650,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":53760,"cache_write_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1625,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":189},"total_tokens":60275,"attribution":{"items":{"fc_0bfe6e1fa8f24ccf016adb3b0a8810819191ac5c11c35bea1b":{"input_t